    "Clinical guidelines focus on issues related to chronic coronary artery disease, chronic kidney disease, and associated conditions. Common interventions include percutaneous coronary intervention (PCI) and coronary artery bypass grafting (CABG). Factors like frailty, nutritional status, and sarcopenia are significant in managing elderly patients with coronary diseases. The impact of kidney disease on cardiovascular health is highlighted, with emphasis on risk prediction and management strategies. Additionally, the effectiveness of lifestyle modifications like exercise-based rehabilitation is considered for long-term outcomes.": [],
